--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
World of Skatecraft and benilla
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This repository is a modified copy of World of Skatecraft by Kimmo3223
(https://github.com/Kimmo3223/world-of-skatecraft), itself a modified copy of
benilla, a from-scratch World of Warcraft 1.12.1 client in Rust and Bevy, by
samwhosung and contributors: https://github.com/samwhosung/benilla

benilla is licensed under the MIT license or the Apache License 2.0, at your
option (LICENSE-MIT, LICENSE-APACHE). Those terms cover benilla's code and the
changes to it here, except where a file or crate says otherwise.

Files changed from benilla (by World of Skatecraft, and since by World of
Kartcraft): the kart mode in crates/benilla-app/src/kart/, its hooks in
crates/benilla-app/src/player/{controller,state}.rs,
crates/benilla-app/src/{lib,game_plugins,creature_anim}.rs,
crates/benilla-app/src/creature_anim/driver.rs (the seated pose in the kart),
crates/benilla-app/Cargo.toml, the KeyBoneID and accessor additions in
crates/benilla-assets/src/model.rs, crates/benilla-world/src/rig_anim.rs,
crates/benilla-world/src/rig_anim/{pose,global_seq}.rs and
crates/benilla-world/src/collision/one_sided.rs (with the matching field in
benilla's test fixtures), crates/benilla-world/src/boot.rs (gamepads on),
crates/benilla-world/src/worldview.rs (the demo's hook), the Karting
profession's client data in crates/benilla-formats/src/{kartcraft,chain,lib}.rs,
the schedule and world-API ratchets (game_plugins.rs, tests/world_api_wall.rs),
.github/, plus tools/, setup/, the play and demo scripts and these docs.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Crash Team Racing: the driving model and the kart
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

crates/ctr-kart is a Rust port of Crash Team Racing's kart physics, written
from the decompilation of the NTSC-U game by CTR-tools and contributors:
https://github.com/CTR-tools/ctr-native and
https://github.com/CTR-tools/CTR-ModSDK (GNU General Public License v3.0).
docs/ctr-physics-spec.md records what was read and where.

crates/ctr-assets reads the player's own CTR disc image (ISO 9660, BIGFILE,
.ctr models, VRAM textures), following the format work of DCxDemo's CTR-tools
(https://github.com/CTR-tools/CTR-tools, GNU General Public License v2.0) and
the decompilation; docs/ctr-assets.md documents the formats.

These crates, and crates/kartcraft and crates/kart-demo which build on them,
are licensed under the GNU General Public License, version 3 or later
(LICENSE-GPL-3.0). A build
of the game that includes them is therefore distributed under GPL-3.0-or-later
as a whole (MIT and Apache-2.0 are compatible with it).

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Tools used by setup (not included)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

vmangos (https://github.com/vmangos/core) and vmangos-deploy
(https://github.com/mserajnik/vmangos-deploy) run the local server; setup
downloads them from their own sources.

setup/vmangos/kartcraft.patch is a patch to vmangos that adds the Karting
profession (adapted from World of Skatecraft's Skateboarding patch); setup
applies it when it builds the server image. Like vmangos, the patch is under
the GNU General Public License, version 2 or later.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Game content
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

No World of Warcraft or Crash Team Racing game data is contained in this
repository or in anything built from it. Players use their own copies: the WoW
1.12.1 client is read at runtime, and setup converts the player's own CTR disc
image on their machine into kart-data/, which is never committed.
